// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22).

== greet
? endgame time:morning
- {hi}! Why did the cadet stay? For the tea! Ha! No, that's the whole joke.   #funny

== chat
? endgame
- Lovely news. Lovely. Have you eaten? It's a scone sort of news.   #warm
- Your mug's still on its hook. I'd got the paper out to wrap it. So glad I didn't.   #warm
- No more promotion teas, so I've invented Tuesday tea. It's the same tea. On a Tuesday.   #funny
- Brennan's given me an oven on Sunday. Says it's for you. I needed a visa. You're my visa.   #funny

== bye
? endgame
- Off you go. Mind the rack on the way out, the end hook bites. Lovely.
